  "notes": [
    "packaged-* cases: the input files benchmarks.json and families.json are the files v0.4.0 ships in src/oah/templates/engines; score_set reads them. `choices` keys are tier/floor/profile; each value is the Choice with the candidate band, or {\"error\": code}. Scores are IEEE doubles as Python prints them; compare with a tolerance of 1e-9.",
    "precedence-* cases: map_tier for every tier. `effort_ok` lists the models the effort rules allow (null: no rules). `pins` maps a tier to its pinned model. `scores` null means no score set.",
    "epoch-csv-* error cases: epoch_scores raises DataError, which has no code; its only caller (fetch_epoch) turns it into a failed refresh, reported as OAH_SCORES_REFRESH_FAILED, so that is the code given.",
    "Table cases give `calls` (row name -> arguments) and expect a map of row name -> result."
  ],
  "omitted": [
